1.explanation:
In report-generator.js (v2), the code in generateReportHtml does

    const sanitizedJavascript = REPORT_JAVASCRIPT.replace(/<\//g, '\\u003c/');
    return REPORT_TEMPLATE
      .replace(/%%LIGHTHOUSE_JSON%%/, sanitizedJson)
      .replace(/%%LIGHTHOUSE_JAVASCRIPT%%/, sanitizedJavascript);

Using String.replace(regex, replacementString) treats `$` in the replacement as special tokens (e.g. `$'`). When REPORT_JAVASCRIPT contains `$'`, replace will inject the post-match text instead of the literal `$'`, mangling the HTML. To fix this, every `$` in sanitizedJavascript must be escaped (e.g. `sanitizedJavascript.replace(/\$/g, '$$$$')`) or the code should use the callback form of replace so that the script is inserted unparsed.
